     4	//! `ZombieHorse`, `SkeletonHorse`. See `designs/equine-framework.md` for the design rationale.
     5	//!
     6	//! Phase 1 scope: taming, feeding, chest inventory, breeding attribute inheritance,
     7	//! `randomizeAttributes`, sounds. Rider-controlled movement (`PlayerRideableJumping`,
     8	//! mounted-input routing) is out of scope -- a horse can be saddled and mounted, but does
     9	//! not yet respond to WASD/jump while ridden.
    10	//!
    11	//! Deliberate simplifications versus vanilla, noted here once rather than at every call site:
    12	//! - Saddle/body-armor equipping is done directly in `abstract_horse_mob_interact` (mirroring
    13	//!   `HappyGhastEntity::try_equip_harness`) rather than through a generic
    14	//!   `ItemStack.interactLivingEntity` dispatch, which doesn't exist in Pumpkin yet.
    15	//! - The chest inventory screen is opened via the existing generic-container screen handler
    16	//!   (`create_generic_9x3`), not a ported `HorseInventoryMenu`/`ClientboundMountScreenOpenPacket`.
    17	//!   Vanilla's real screen has dedicated saddle/armor slots plus the chest columns in one menu;
    18	//!   here the saddle/armor stay equipment-slot-only (no slot in the chest GUI) and only the
    19	//!   chest storage is shown. This is a real, working inventory (right-click+sneak on a tamed
    20	//!   chested horse opens and persists chest contents) but is not pixel-identical to vanilla's
    21	//!   menu layout -- flagged as a follow-up if the exact vanilla GUI is required.
    22	//! - The shared `mob_tick` hook now handles the server-side grazing trigger and standing timer;
    23	//!   species-specific hooks call it before their own extra per-tick behavior.
